      "content": "Approaching the discussion in a way that emphasizes the historical context of Conrad's time can be a great approach. By saying that the language reflects the attitudes of the era, you can frame it as a product of its time without necessarily condoning or endorsing those attitudes. This allows you to acknowledge the complexity of the text without lecturing or judging the students, and instead, invites them to analyze and think critically about the ways in which literature can reveal the ideologies of its time.",
